          "arguments": "{\"outcome\":\"compromise\",\"summary\":\"I couldn't put the drawer and the spike at the same corner. The configurator refuses that with SPIKE_CLASH: the drawer fills the corner where the spike would have to stand.\\n\\nWhat I built instead: a north-half base at 1,0,0 with one drawer on its cut face (drawer:0#1,0#cut). Full bases sit around it at 0,0,0, 1,-1,0, 2,-1,0 and 2,0,0. The one spike (spike:0#1,-1|1,0|2,-1) is at a different corner of the half base's cell: the north-east corner where cells 1,-1, 1,0 and 2,-1 meet, so it isn't at the drawer's corner and doesn't touch the drawer.\\n\\nI ran lockJoints and it bolted the joints. capOpenFaces was refused because a cap would run 5 mm into the drawer frame (MESH_CLASH), so the open faces are uncapped. check_build passes with no rule errors and the collision check reads clear.\",\"requirements\":[{\"requirement\":\"One drawer\",\"status\":\"met\",\"evidence\":\"drawer:0#1,0#cut on the cut face of the half base at 1,0,0.\"},{\"requirement\":\"One spike\",\"status\":\"met\",\"evidence\":\"spike:0#1,-1|1,0|2,-1.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Drawer and spike at the very same corner of the same cell, touching\",\"status\":\"unmet\",\"evidence\":\"The configurator refused a spike at junction 1,0 / 2,-1 / 2,0 with SPIKE_CLASH because the drawer fills that corner. The spike stands at another corner of the same cell (1,-1 / 1,0 / 2,-1) instead, and it doesn't touch the drawer.\"},{\"requirement\":\"House rules (caps and locked joints)\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"lockJoints added joint bolts. capOpenFaces was refused because a cap would run into the drawer frame (MESH_CLASH), so the open faces are uncapped.\"}]}"
